1
00:00:09,204 --> 00:00:12,742
If all this is empty, nothing
arises and nothing ends.

2
00:00:12,822 --> 00:00:17,145
Nāgārjuna put the strongest objection
to his own view in his own book.

3
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:18,589
And then he answered it.

4
00:00:19,384 --> 00:00:22,012
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:22,092 --> 00:00:25,970
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:31,297
Over six sections I have argued that
nothing appears with a nature of its own.

7
00:00:31,377 --> 00:00:33,770
Not the apple. Not the moment.

8
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:37,234
Not mind, not matter, not
the links of the chain.

9
00:00:37,314 --> 00:00:40,581
A view that says this will
meet objections, and it should.

10
00:00:41,376 --> 00:00:43,284
Some come from philosophers.

11
00:00:43,364 --> 00:00:44,928
Some from scientists.

12
00:00:45,008 --> 00:00:46,572
Some from other Buddhists.

13
00:00:46,652 --> 00:00:49,729
And some from one's own mind,
at three in the morning.

14
00:00:50,524 --> 00:00:52,717
Nāgārjuna did not avoid them.

15
00:00:52,797 --> 00:00:56,033
He gives the opponent's case,
in the opponent's words,

16
00:00:56,113 --> 00:00:59,049
for six verses, before he replies.

17
00:00:59,129 --> 00:01:01,223
That is the method I want to follow.

18
00:01:01,303 --> 00:01:03,709
State each objection at its strongest.

19
00:01:03,789 --> 00:01:07,273
Then answer it on its
own terms. There are six.

20
00:01:08,072 --> 00:01:10,691
The first. This is nihilism.

21
00:01:11,484 --> 00:01:15,335
If nothing has a nature of its
own, then nothing really exists.

22
00:01:15,415 --> 00:01:18,542
If nothing really exists,
nothing really matters.

23
00:01:18,622 --> 00:01:21,721
Not suffering, not kindness, not the path.

24
00:01:21,801 --> 00:01:25,027
Emptiness, followed
honestly, ends in a shrug.

25
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:28,550
Nāgārjuna's opponent says it exactly.

26
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:32,843
If all this is empty, there is
no arising and no passing away,

27
00:01:32,923 --> 00:01:35,592
and the four noble truths do not exist.

28
00:01:36,404 --> 00:01:38,910
He turns it round, word for word.

29
00:01:38,990 --> 00:01:43,557
If all this were not empty, there would
be no arising and no passing away.

30
00:01:43,637 --> 00:01:47,243
Then it is for you that the four
noble truths would not exist.

31
00:01:48,048 --> 00:01:50,672
A thing with its own
nature could not arise,

32
00:01:50,752 --> 00:01:55,744
because it would already be what it is.
It could not change. It could not end.

33
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:59,005
Suffering with its own nature
could never be relieved.

34
00:01:59,085 --> 00:02:01,980
A path with its own nature
could never be walked.

35
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:06,224
It is the world of own natures
that is frozen, not the empty one.

36
00:02:07,036 --> 00:02:09,718
And the shrug rests on
what it claims to deny.

37
00:02:09,798 --> 00:02:14,365
It is all empty, so it doesn't matter,
only works if mattering needs a solid

38
00:02:14,445 --> 00:02:19,284
core. That is the same assumption as the
eternalist's, mourned instead of kept.

39
00:02:19,364 --> 00:02:23,459
Something can be cut off only if it
was there from its own side first.

40
00:02:24,272 --> 00:02:28,232
The person who is not found is
the person who keeps the promise.

41
00:02:29,052 --> 00:02:31,630
The second. Then it is all mind.

42
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:35,286
You have taken away the hard
little things out there.

43
00:02:35,366 --> 00:02:38,478
What is left is appearing: sights, sounds,

44
00:02:38,558 --> 00:02:40,965
feelings, all vivid, all known.

45
00:02:41,045 --> 00:02:43,931
Surely, then, everything is mind.

46
00:02:44,732 --> 00:02:49,425
This is the most natural next step, and
I have watched it happen many times.

47
00:02:49,505 --> 00:02:52,591
The producer is gone. The hearer is gone.

48
00:02:52,671 --> 00:02:55,499
And mind is left standing
as what everything is.

49
00:02:55,579 --> 00:02:58,778
That is the ground coming
back, this time as mind.

50
00:02:59,592 --> 00:03:02,406
But the ringing of a bell is
there only with the bronze,

51
00:03:02,486 --> 00:03:04,815
the strike, the air and the ear.

52
00:03:04,895 --> 00:03:08,149
Being dependent, it is not
mind from its own side,

53
00:03:08,292 --> 00:03:11,002
any more than it is
bronze from its own side.

54
00:03:11,812 --> 00:03:14,522
Clarity is never absent from what appears.

55
00:03:14,602 --> 00:03:17,783
But lifted out, and made
what everything is made of,

56
00:03:17,863 --> 00:03:19,630
it is one more reification.

57
00:03:19,710 --> 00:03:23,122
When matter is seen through,
the habit does not give up.

58
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:24,739
It changes its stuff.

59
00:03:24,819 --> 00:03:28,099
Matter stuff traded for
mind stuff is still stuff.

60
00:03:28,904 --> 00:03:33,221
The third. Then it is only
concepts, and anything goes.

61
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:37,681
If everything is named in
dependence, then it is all labels.

62
00:03:37,761 --> 00:03:39,488
Labels are ours to choose.

63
00:03:39,568 --> 00:03:42,087
So any view is as good as any other.

64
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:46,527
Designation is not arbitrary,
and it is not free.

65
00:03:46,607 --> 00:03:48,918
It works, and it can be wrong.

66
00:03:48,998 --> 00:03:51,079
A forged passport fails.

67
00:03:51,159 --> 00:03:54,774
A mistaken face in a crowd
is corrected when it turns.

68
00:03:54,854 --> 00:03:58,624
A rope seen as a snake in dim
light is put right by a lamp.

69
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:01,477
Tsongkhapa gives three tests.

70
00:04:01,558 --> 00:04:03,638
Is it known to ordinary cognition?

71
00:04:03,718 --> 00:04:06,736
Is it not overturned by
further ordinary cognition?

72
00:04:06,816 --> 00:04:09,793
Is it not contradicted by
analysis of the ultimate?

73
00:04:09,873 --> 00:04:12,266
The snake in the rope fails the second.

74
00:04:12,346 --> 00:04:15,160
The rope with its own
nature fails the third.

75
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:18,479
The rope, as named, passes all three.

76
00:04:19,296 --> 00:04:23,306
Conventional truth, for me, is the
only kind of validity there is,

77
00:04:23,386 --> 00:04:28,301
and it is fully valid. Merely conventional
was never meant as merely made up.

78
00:04:29,116 --> 00:04:33,134
The fourth. Dissolving the
Hard Problem is not solving it.

79
00:04:33,944 --> 00:04:38,470
Philosophers have asked for decades how
physical processes give rise to felt

80
00:04:38,550 --> 00:04:41,749
experience. You say the
question falls away.

81
00:04:41,829 --> 00:04:43,746
But the mystery is still there.

82
00:04:43,826 --> 00:04:47,052
Why does this brain activity
go with this taste of coffee?

83
00:04:47,868 --> 00:04:52,004
I want to be careful here, because
the objection is partly right.

84
00:04:52,816 --> 00:04:57,220
What falls away is one question: how does
a stuff whose nature is to lack feeling

85
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,819
produce a stuff whose nature is to feel?

86
00:04:59,899 --> 00:05:02,564
That question needs
two banks and a bridge.

87
00:05:02,644 --> 00:05:07,143
And the banks were built by the framework
that defined mind and matter as inherently

88
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:10,363
different. A third
substrate does not help.

89
00:05:10,443 --> 00:05:14,185
It only pushes the problem up a
level, and calls it the ground.

90
00:05:14,996 --> 00:05:18,467
What does not fall away is the
ordinary, workable question.

91
00:05:18,547 --> 00:05:22,366
Which conditions go with which
experiences, and how reliably.

92
00:05:22,446 --> 00:05:26,890
Which part of the brain, which
chemical, which training, which injury.

93
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:30,251
That work is real, and nothing
here stands in its way.

94
00:05:31,056 --> 00:05:34,173
I am not offering a theory
of how matter makes mind.

95
00:05:34,253 --> 00:05:37,407
I am saying that the demand
for one rested on a picture.

96
00:05:37,487 --> 00:05:42,316
Without the picture, what is left is
not a mystery, but a field of study.

97
00:05:43,132 --> 00:05:46,525
The fifth. The physics is being stretched.

98
00:05:47,336 --> 00:05:51,119
Every few years someone finds
the Buddha in quantum mechanics.

99
00:05:51,199 --> 00:05:55,331
Physicists object, rightly, that their
theories are about measurements and

100
00:05:55,411 --> 00:05:58,053
mathematics, not about emptiness.

101
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,401
I agree with the caution.

102
00:06:00,481 --> 00:06:06,461
In Section 1, I set two physicists beside
dependent arising as echoes, not proofs.

103
00:06:06,541 --> 00:06:11,357
Emptiness does not depend on physics,
and physics does not prove emptiness.

104
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:14,177
I also said where I part from them.

105
00:06:14,257 --> 00:06:19,027
If relations become what is really real,
or a field becomes the new substance,

106
00:06:19,107 --> 00:06:23,063
then physics has been used to rebuild
exactly what dependent arising takes

107
00:06:23,143 --> 00:06:24,343
apart.

108
00:06:24,788 --> 00:06:27,036
What I take from physics is modest.

109
00:06:27,116 --> 00:06:30,759
Even our best descriptions of
matter do not show finished things,

110
00:06:30,839 --> 00:06:35,722
waiting to be measured. The view stands
or falls on looking, not on any theory.

111
00:06:36,528 --> 00:06:41,104
The sixth. Then emptiness, or
the web, is the new absolute.

112
00:06:41,908 --> 00:06:43,463
You deny every ground.

113
00:06:43,543 --> 00:06:45,365
But you keep saying emptiness.

114
00:06:45,445 --> 00:06:47,104
Isn't emptiness your ground?

115
00:06:47,184 --> 00:06:50,433
Or the web of relations, connecting
everything to everything.

116
00:06:50,513 --> 00:06:52,584
Isn't that the real thing at last?

117
00:06:53,384 --> 00:06:55,333
Nāgārjuna saw this coming.

118
00:06:55,413 --> 00:06:58,444
Emptiness was taught as
the way out of all views.

119
00:06:58,524 --> 00:07:02,470
But those for whom emptiness
becomes a view, he called incurable.

120
00:07:03,276 --> 00:07:06,094
Emptiness is not a thing behind things.

121
00:07:06,174 --> 00:07:09,899
It is the absence of what was
never there: a nature of their own.

122
00:07:09,979 --> 00:07:13,961
Taken as a void, a state to
reach, or a view to defend,

123
00:07:14,041 --> 00:07:16,873
it has become the next
object of the old habit.

124
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:21,993
The web is the same. Relations are
named together with what they relate.

125
00:07:22,073 --> 00:07:26,477
A connection between two things that have
no standing of their own is not a third

126
00:07:26,557 --> 00:07:30,716
thing with standing. The relating
is as empty as what it relates.

127
00:07:30,796 --> 00:07:32,840
And it works exactly as well.

128
00:07:33,644 --> 00:07:37,291
Most of these objections are
not only out there, in books.

129
00:07:37,371 --> 00:07:42,237
They arise in my own mind. Then
nothing matters. Then it is all mind.

130
00:07:42,317 --> 00:07:44,248
Then it is all just labels.

131
00:07:44,328 --> 00:07:49,225
Each comes with a small sense of relief,
as if a floor had been found at last.

132
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:54,502
When one comes, I find it useful to
ask what it is relieved to have found.

133
00:07:54,582 --> 00:07:56,242
Usually it is a ground.

134
00:07:56,322 --> 00:08:00,825
Something to stand on, or something
to give up on. Neither is needed.

135
00:08:01,636 --> 00:08:05,686
This is Section 7, Part 2 of
the Dependent Arising series,

136
00:08:05,766 --> 00:08:07,539
and the close of the series.

137
00:08:08,336 --> 00:08:10,611
The bell still rings when it is struck.

